From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xinput: scan an empty slot's device list at most once a
 second

XInputGetState on a slot with no device scanned the HID device list
under xinput_cs on every call: SetupDiGetClassDevsW and its registry
keys, a wineserver open_key each time. Portal 2 polls its pads every
frame, and with one pad connected the empty slots cost about 3.7
open_key requests a frame on the game's main thread.

The update thread already adds an arriving device when it is notified
and rescans every 2 s when no report arrives, so the scan in
xinput_get_state is a fallback for a missed notification. Run it only
when the last scan of anyone is a second old. The first poll still
scans, because the update thread scans before start_update_thread
returns. XInputSetState and XInputGetCapabilities keep their scan.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-05-portal2-hitches-requests.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/xinput1_3/main.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c b/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c
index f56c164..e52dedc 100644
--- a/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c
+++ b/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c
@@ -517,6 +517,9 @@ static void try_remove_device(const WCHAR *device_path)
         controller_destroy(&controllers[i], FALSE);
 }
 
+/* GetTickCount() of the last HID device list scan, xinput_cs must be held */
+static DWORD list_scan_tick;
+
 static void update_controller_list(void)
 {
     char buffer[sizeof(SP_DEVICE_INTERFACE_DETAIL_DATA_W) + MAX_PATH * sizeof(WCHAR)];
@@ -528,6 +531,7 @@ static void update_controller_list(void)
 
     EnterCriticalSection(&xinput_cs);
 
+    list_scan_tick = GetTickCount();
     set = SetupDiGetClassDevsW(&guid, NULL, NULL, DIGCF_DEVICEINTERFACE | DIGCF_PRESENT);
     detail->cbSize = sizeof(*detail);
 
@@ -909,8 +913,12 @@ static DWORD xinput_get_state(DWORD index, XINPUT_STATE *state)
 
     if (get_current_state(index, state)) return ERROR_SUCCESS;
 
+    /* A game polls every slot each frame, and a scan of the device list
+     * costs registry round trips through setupapi. The update thread adds
+     * an arriving device when it is notified and rescans every 2 s, so a
+     * slot with no device scans again here at most once a second. */
     EnterCriticalSection(&xinput_cs);
-    update_controller_list();
+    if (GetTickCount() - list_scan_tick >= 1000) update_controller_list();
     ret = get_current_state(index, state) ? ERROR_SUCCESS : ERROR_DEVICE_NOT_CONNECTED;
     LeaveCriticalSection(&xinput_cs);
 
